        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***SUPERB SEMI-DETACHED PROPERTY / SOUGHT AFTER LOCATION / BAY WINDOWS / ORIGINAL FEATURES / 151SQM***\r\n\r\nKELLY BRADSHAW are delighted to present No. 64 Glasnevin Avenue, Glasnevin, Dublin 11 to the market, a substantial four-bedroom family home extending to approximately 151 sq. metres. \r\n\r\nThe subject property is part of a large site which is divided into two lots with planning permission for a detached 2 bedroom residence to side. A map of the divide is attached to the brochure. No 64, the original building, will retain a side passage to the rear garden as per the map provided and in addition to this will have an L shaped extended garden to the rear also. This will facilate rear vehicular access subject to planning permission. \r\n\r\nOffering wonderfully spacious and versatile accommodation over two levels, No. 64 is a home bursting with potential. The generous proportions, excellent room sizes and superb site provide the perfect ingredients for purchasers wishing to create a truly special family home in this highly regarded Dublin 11 location.\r\n\r\nOn entering the property, you are greeted by a spacious entrance hallway with timber flooring and staircase leading to the upper level. To the front is a bright and inviting living room, a wonderfully comfortable reception space featuring timber flooring, a large picture window and an attractive feature fireplace creating a natural focal point within the room.\r\n\r\nThe separate dining room is another particularly generous reception room, enjoying excellent natural light through a wide window overlooking the garden. With its timber flooring and excellent proportions, this is an ideal space for family dining and entertaining.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, the accommodation opens into a spacious family room, providing a relaxed everyday living space adjoining the kitchen. The kitchen itself is fitted with an extensive range of units and incorporates a breakfast bar, while direct access leads out to the rear garden. A bathroom and additional hall area complete this section of the accommodation.\r\n\r\nA particularly useful feature of the ground floor is the fourth bedroom, positioned separately from the main upstairs sleeping accommodation. Extending to approximately 5.76m in length, this versatile room could equally lend itself to use as a home office, playroom, additional reception room or guest accommodation depending on the requirements of the new owners.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, including an impressive primary bedroom measuring approximately 3.36m x 4.32m. The remaining bedrooms are also bright and comfortable, while a family bathroom and landing complete the upper-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, No. 64 benefits from a generous private garden, offering excellent outdoor space for families, gardening and entertaining. The garden provides a wonderful extension of the living accommodation. The combination of substantial internal accommodation and generous external space is a particularly appealing feature of this family home.\r\n\r\nThe location is another major selling point. Glasnevin Avenue is a mature and highly convenient residential setting in Dublin 11, with an excellent selection of everyday amenities within easy reach. Glasnevin, Drumcondra and Santry are all readily accessible, providing a wide choice of shops, cafés, restaurants and services, while the area is particularly well served by primary and secondary schools. DCU, the National Botanic Gardens, Albert College Park and a host of sporting and recreational facilities are also nearby.\r\n\r\nTransport connections are excellent, with numerous bus routes serving the surrounding area and providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre. The M1, M50 and Dublin Airport are also easily accessible, making the location particularly convenient for commuters and those travelling further afield.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing comes highly recommended."
      },
